dated strictly, so an older CLI rejects a field it does not know. When a project is shared, upgrade its CLI development dependency before running a newer CLI's commands on it."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[["A change to the meaning or shape of an existing field increments ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["schemaVersion"]},". The CLI release that introduces it upgrades older files as part of a normal, previewed command, and refuses files from a newer version instead of guessing."]]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":["There is no hosted JSON Schema URL yet; none will be referenced from the file until one is published."]},"\n"]]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Because the exact CLI version is a development dependency of the project, everyone working on it runs the same CLI and reads the file the same way."]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"next-steps"},"children":["Next steps"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","props":{},"children":[["\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"installation.md"},"children":["Install the CLI"]},"."]]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"commands.md"},"children":["Read the command reference"]},"."]]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"skills.md"},"children":["Manage skills and conflicts"]},"."]]},"\n"]]}],"toc":[{"title":"How the format evolves","url":"#how-the-format-evolves","depth":2},{"title":"Next steps","url":"#next-steps","depth":2}]}